Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 08:40:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cps2w: the vsavjw catalogue entry re-pointed to merged-m20
 (14z-183)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

jtframe's .rom builder locates every zip member by CRC32 and by nothing else
(mra2rom.go:163-172, no name fallback), so the machine entry must name the
CRCs of the actual build or the MRA produces no .rom at all. Regenerated from
build/m3b_merged28/rompath/vsavjw.zip (sha1 34a76669) by tools/gen_vsavjw_xml.py
in the consuming tree; --check now reports the catalogue matches the build.

FOUR members moved, and they are the M20 delta exactly:
  vm3j.04d  02aba291 -> 3e4098b8   program: the #157 throw-meter fix — the
  vsw.41    7102a42c -> c47529fa   tenants' copies of the hit-registration
                                   stores re-pointed from the dead vs2 pair to
                                   the live pair (Donovan in vm3j.04d, Phobos
                                   and Pyron in the extension)
  vsw.33m   6f5a1c98 -> 70bc7941   group-C glyphs, the M19 -> M20 mark
  vsw.37m   60b51461 -> aba94e63   likewise

No RTL, no cfg, no core change: doc/mame.xml only. cores/cps1, cores/cps2 and
cores/cps15 remain byte-untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KhMsPBCKQPWahuq6rrzsLw
